        <h3>The GitOps Workflow</h3>
        <p>
          With the Bootstrap Pattern, deployments follow a simple flow: push
          YAML to Git, ArgoCD syncs automatically. No more
          <code>kubectl apply</code> commands.
        </p>
        <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b">
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 text-left font-medium">Directory</th>
                <th class="py-2 text-left font-medium">Contents</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-border/50 border-b">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>apps/</code></td>
                <td class="py-2"
                  >Application manifests (Deployments, Services)</td
                >
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-border/50 border-b">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>infrastructure/</code></td>
                <td class="py-2"
                  >System manifests (monitoring, ingress, storage)</td
                >
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-border/50 border-b">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>argocd/</code></td>
                <td class="py-2"
                  >Application CRDs (pointers to the above folders)</td
                >
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <details class="mt-4">
          <summary
            class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground cursor-pointer text-sm"
            >The Bootstrap Pattern Explained</summary
          >
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-4 text-sm">
            <p>
              The magic happens through a recursive pattern. You apply one file
              manually. Everything else happens automatically.
            </p>

            <p><strong>Step 1: Apply bootstrap.yaml once</strong></p>
            <pre
              class="bg-secondary overflow-x-auto rounded-md p-3 text-xs"
            ><code>apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: bootstrap
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/your/repo
    path: argocd/              # Watch this folder
  destination:
    namespace: argocd
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true</code></pre>

            <p><strong>Step 2: ArgoCD reads argocd/ folder</strong></p>
            <p>
              Inside <code>argocd/</code> are more Application CRDs. For
              example, <code>argocd/monitoring.yaml</code>:
            </p>
            <pre
              class="bg-secondary overflow-x-auto rounded-md p-3 text-xs"
            ><code>apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: monitoring
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/your/repo
    path: infrastructure/monitoring/  # Points to manifests
  destination:
    namespace: monitoring
  syncPolicy:
    automated: {}</code></pre>

            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              <strong>The result:</strong> Bootstrap creates Applications that
              create more Applications. You push to Git, ArgoCD syncs
              everything. No more manual kubectl apply commands.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
